.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int32_t schultz_audio_create (\fBschultz_audio\fP ** out_audio)"

.PP
Starts the audio system\&. Opens nothing yet: a device is opened when the first thing wants to play, so an application that creates this and never plays anything costs nothing\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIout_audio\fP Receives the system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY, or SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when the platform has no audio at all\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void schultz_audio_destroy (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio)"

.PP
Stops everything and releases it\&. Every sound, stream and recorder made from this system goes with it, so a host does not have to take them down in order\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system, or NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_audio_set_volume (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, float volume)"

.PP
Sets the volume everything is scaled by, from zero to one\&. Applied on top of each sound's or stream's own volume, so one call quiets an application without disturbing the balance inside it\&. Above one is allowed and will distort, which is the platform's business rather than this one's\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIvolume\fP Zero for silence, one for as recorded\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "float schultz_audio_volume (const \fBschultz_audio\fP * audio)"

.PP
Returns the volume everything is scaled by\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. NULL yields zero\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The volume last set, or one\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint32_t schultz_audio_output_count (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio)"

.PP
Counts the devices sound can be played to, and lists them\&. Calling this settles the list that schultz_audio_device_name and schultz_audio_device_id read from, so ask for the count first and then walk it\&. Asking again, for either kind, replaces the list\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. NULL yields zero\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
How many there are\&. 
.RE
.PP

