.SS "int32_t schultz_audio_set_output (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, uint64_t device)"

.PP
Says which device sound is played to\&. Zero, which is what a system starts with, means whatever the platform calls the default\&. That is the better answer on a phone: it follows the platform when a headset is plugged in or pulled out, without an application doing anything\&.
.PP
\fBWhat is already open stays where it is\&.\fP This decides where the next stream, sound or decoder opens, so an application changing device recreates what it wants moved\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIdevice\fP A number from schultz_audio_device_id, or zero for the default\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

