\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIdevice\fP A number from schultz_audio_device_id, or zero for the default\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint64_t schultz_audio_input (const \fBschultz_audio\fP * audio)"

.PP
Returns the device the microphone is read from, or zero\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. NULL yields zero\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The device number, or zero\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_audio_devices_changed (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio)"

.PP
Reports whether the devices have changed since this was last asked\&. A headset arriving or leaving changes what an application should be offering in its settings\&. Asked rather than announced, like everything else here: a host that has a window checks this on a turn of its loop, and one with no window checks it whenever it likes\&.
.PP
The first call after the system is made reports a change, because there was nothing to compare against\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. NULL yields zero\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Nonzero when the list of devices is not what it was\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_sound_load_file (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, const char * path, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_sound)"

.PP
Decodes a sound and keeps it, ready to play\&. For anything short and played often: a click, an alert, a chime\&. It is decoded now rather than while it plays, because a sound decoded again on every press is work done twice for nothing\&.
.PP
WAV, AIFF, VOC and AU, plus MP3, FLAC and Ogg Vorbis\&. What is deliberately absent is MOD, MIDI and the console formats, whose decoders are copyleft or need a set of instruments shipped with them; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES\&.md\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIpath\fP The file\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIout_sound\fP Receives the sound\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY, SCHULTZ_ERR_UNREADABLE when the file is missing or is not something this build decodes, or SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when no device would open\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_sound_load_memory (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, const void * bytes, uint64_t length, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_sound)"

.PP
The same, from bytes already in memory\&. For a sound that arrived over a network or was built into the program\&. The bytes are decoded during the call and are the host's again afterwards\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIbytes\fP The file's contents\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIlength\fP How many bytes\&. 
.br
\fIout_sound\fP Receives the sound\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
As schultz_sound_load_file\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_sound_play (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, \fBschultz_handle\fP sound)"

.PP
Plays a sound, over anything already playing\&. The same sound may be playing several times at once, which is what a run of key presses sounds like\&. There are eight places to play at a time, and asking for a ninth says so rather than cutting off one that can be heard\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIsound\fP A sound from schultz_sound_load_file or _load_memory\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE, or SCHULTZ_ERR_EXHAUSTED when every place is busy\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_sound_stop (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, \fBschultz_handle\fP sound)"

