.SS "int32_t schultz_music_play (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, const char * path, int32_t repeats)"

.PP
Plays a long piece of music, decoded as it goes\&. One at a time: asking for another replaces what is playing\&. Unlike a sound it is not held in memory, because minutes of samples is tens of megabytes and nothing is gained by keeping them\&.
