.SS "int32_t schultz_audio_recorder_create (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, uint32_t format, uint32_t channels, uint32_t rate, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_recorder)"

.PP
Opens the microphone\&. \fBThe platform has to allow it\&.\fP iOS refuses without NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in the application's Info\&.plist and asks the person the first time; Android needs RECORD_AUDIO in the manifest and a request while running\&. Neither is something the toolkit can do on an application's behalf, and where permission is missing this fails rather than recording silence\&.
.PP
Nothing is captured until schultz_audio_recorder_start\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIformat\fP SCHULTZ_AUDIO_S16 or SCHULTZ_AUDIO_F32\&. 
.br
\fIchannels\fP One for mono, two for stereo\&. 
.br
\fIrate\fP Samples per second\&. 
.br
\fIout_recorder\fP Receives the recorder\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY, or SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when there is no microphone or no permission to use it\&. 
.RE
.PP

