.SS "int32_t schultz_audio_recorder_save (\fBschultz_audio\fP * audio, \fBschultz_handle\fP recorder, const char * path)"

.PP
Writes what the microphone makes straight into a WAV file\&. For recording rather than listening\&. The toolkit takes the samples as the device produces them and writes them out, so nothing has to be read on a clock and nothing is lost while an application is busy\&.
.PP
\fBSaving and reading are two ways to the same bytes\&.\fP While a recorder is saving, the toolkit drains it, so schultz_audio_recorder_read has nothing to give\&. An application picks one\&.
.PP
The file is a WAV of exactly what was asked for at schultz_audio_recorder_create\&. Its header is written when the file opens and corrected when it closes, so a file left behind by a crash still opens, with whatever had been written by then\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIaudio\fP The system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIrecorder\fP A recorder from schultz_audio_recorder_create\&. 
.br
\fIpath\fP Where to write\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE, SCHULTZ_ERR_EXHAUSTED when it is already saving somewhere, or SCHULTZ_ERR_UNREADABLE when the file could not be opened\&. 
.RE
.PP

